# Compiled Python bytecode is build cruft here, never a fixture: every .pyc this
# package ever grew had its .py source beside it. `COPY . /tests` would bake it
# into the verifier image and move the tests/ content hash that tags that image.
#
# Patterns are given in both forms deliberately. Docker's ignore matching does
# not cross `/`, so a bare `__pycache__` or `*.pyc` covers only the context root
# and misses nested directories -- the same blind spot that `find -maxdepth 1`
# had, which is why this class stayed invisible to the packages' own gates.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
